From e17010f1068c3384b7b5efc92e33da560d6b3eed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:11:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(profile): keep avatar circle fixed for non-square
 photos, add drag/zoom crop

The circular avatar frame in ProfileNew was distorting into an oval for
non-square uploads (e.g. 9:16 portraits): .np-photo used display:grid with
place-items:center, which let a percentage-sized <img> child size its
implicit grid track from the image's own intrinsic aspect ratio instead of
staying a fixed square. Positioning the image absolutely inside its
(already position:relative) parent removes it from grid-track sizing, so
object-fit:cover and border-radius:50% now clip a true circle regardless of
the source photo's aspect ratio.

On top of that, add an Instagram-style adjust step: after picking/compressing
a photo, a modal opens showing it inside the same circular frame, and the
person can drag to pan and use a slider to zoom before confirming. The final
crop is rendered to an 800x800 canvas and only then uploaded, replacing the
previous fully-automatic center-crop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
